 "id": "A04",
 "kind": "echarts",
 "title": "Trusted and untrusted monitoring differ only in who watches",
 "section": "intro",
 "order": 30,
 "caption": "Both protocols score every piece of AI-written code for suspicion and send the top 2% of scores to a human. A trusted monitor is a weaker model we assume can't scheme; an untrusted monitor is stronger but might collude with the model that wrote the code.",
